{
  "_comment": [
    "The phase-1 opponent deck pool. EDIT THIS FILE, not the code.",
    "",
    "Cards are named, never numbered: ids are an engine detail and the registry",
    "has gaps (16, 37, 38). `deck_pool.py` resolves each name through",
    "clash_royale_env.get_all_card_ids(), which filters Evolutions OUT -- that",
    "matters because an Evolution reuses its base card's name verbatim (id 1 and",
    "id 128 are both 'Archers'), so a name is ambiguous over the full registry",
    "and unambiguous over the playable set.",
    "",
    "FIELDS",
    "  cards           exactly 8 distinct registry names. Champions and Heroes are",
    "                  refused: the teacher never activates an ability, so it would",
    "                  play a strictly worse card than the deck is named for.",
    "  archetype       free text, for the read-out only.",
    "  tags            priors, NOT the gate. 'anti_26' marks a deck the human meta",
    "                  calls a direct counter to 2.6 Hog. MEASUREMENT DISAGREES:",
    "                  tagged decks average a 0.589 win rate against the current",
    "                  policy and untagged ones 0.433, so the tags are if anything",
    "                  backwards for THIS engine. They gate nothing.",
    "  prior_win_rate  optional; seeds the PFSP prior. Omit for 0.5. See",
    "                  'measured' below and deck_pool.NEUTRAL_PRIOR.",
    "  prior_win_rate_vs_26hog_2026_09_03",
    "                  PROVENANCE ONLY, not read. The old prior_win_rate values,",
    "                  measured against a TRAINED 2.6 Hog Cycle policy. Renamed",
    "                  2026-09-15 for the from-scratch run on a new deck: for a",
    "                  random-init net they sent the four hardest decks 59.9% of",
    "                  episodes, bought no episode-share benefit over uniform, and",
    "                  a wrongly-HIGH prior self-seals (audit 04, C3). Restore by",
    "                  renaming the key back, only for a policy they describe.",
    "  enabled         false keeps a deck in the file but out of the pool.",
    "",
    "To add a deck: copy a block, change the names, then run",
    "  python_ai/venv/Scripts/python.exe -m python_ai.opponents.deck_pool",
    "which validates every name and prints the resolved pool. Every failure",
    "raises: a silently-dropped deck would still train, against a distribution",
    "this file no longer describes."
  ],
